  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ESTABLISHMENT OF NEW 400KV JASRA SUBSYSTEM in BAHRAIN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is one of most important projects at the second phase of Al-Dur station for the production of electricity and water and it is supporting Bahrain in its position as a world-class infrastructure linking Bahrain with the global economy as part of Economic Vision 2030 for Bahrain, the main objectives of this project can be summarized as follows:



- Expand and strengthen electricity transmission networks required to meet the needs of increase in demand as a result of natural growth, where the Peak Demand growth rate will reach more than 30% by 2030.

- Contributing in transfer part of the electrical energy produced from the second phase of Al-Dur station to all load centers in Bahrain, and to alleviate the other 4 subsystems that are currently highly loaded.

- Contributing in the GCC electrical interconnection project as well as improving the ability to trade energy between the GCC.</narrative>
  </description>
